    <span class="section-label">The process</span>
    <h1>From conversation to launch in <em>about three weeks.</em></h1>
    <p>The whole process runs through five clear steps, with no mystery in the middle and no drawn-out revision rounds. There is no point where the work gets handed off to "someone on the team," because there is no team behind the scenes. The person who picks up your phone call is the same person who writes your site.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:820px">
    <div class="text-center" style="margin-bottom:2rem">
      <span class="section-label">Timeline</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-inline:auto">The whole process, end to end.</h2>
    </div>

    <ol class="timeline">
      <li class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-time">Day 1 &middot; About 20&ndash;30 minutes</span>
        <h3>Discovery call</h3>
        <p>We get on the phone, you tell me what you do, and I figure out what the site needs to accomplish for you. There is no sales pitch in the conversation, no pressure attached to it, and no moment where I say "let me loop in my strategist." If I am not the right fit for what you need, I will tell you so on the call rather than waste either of our time.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>What you do and who you serve</li>
          <li>What is working (or not working) with your current site</li>
          <li>What the new site needs to do, whether that is phone calls, booked jobs, or quote requests</li>
          <li>Timeline, the content you already have, and any questions you bring</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-time">Day 1&ndash;2 &middot; Agreement &amp; kickoff</span>
        <h3>Service agreement and first payment</h3>
        <p>You sign a short one-page service agreement and make your first monthly payment, and I start building the same day. There is no large deposit to hand over up front and no waiting around for a project manager to schedule the work.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Plain-language service agreement emailed to you</li>
          <li>First monthly payment processed securely</li>
          <li>Shared folder created for your logo, photos, and any content</li>
          <li>Design kicks off the same day you sign</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-time">Week 1&ndash;2 &middot; 7&ndash;10 business days</span>
        <h3>Design and build</h3>
        <p>Every line of code is written from scratch for your brand, and you will see a live preview link within the first few days so you can give feedback while the work is still moving. You can ask for as many revisions as you need, because I do not charge per change. AI generators and template shops will tell you the work is done the moment a layout exists, but I do not, because the rounds after the first draft are where most of the work that actually brings calls in gets done.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Design tailored to your industry and services</li>
          <li>Custom code, with no WordPress, no page builders, and no AI templates underneath</li>
          <li>Live preview link to share with your team</li>
          <li>Unlimited revisions until you are happy</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-time">Week 2&ndash;3 &middot; Launch day</span>
        <h3>Launch</h3>
        <p>I point your domain at the hosting, verify everything is live, submit the sitemap to Google and Bing, and email you a plain-language owner's guide that describes what was shipped. You do not need to touch anything technical along the way.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>DNS configured and SSL activated</li>
          <li>Sitemap submitted to Google and Bing</li>
          <li>Local-business schema verified against the site</li>
          <li>Owner's guide emailed to you</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-time">Ongoing &middot; For as long as you are with me</span>
        <h3>Updates, support, and the partnership part</h3>
        <p>This is the part most agencies skip. After launch I stay with the work, and when something on your end changes (new hours, a new service, a new photo, a seasonal promo) you simply email or text me, and the change tends to land quickly on most business days. I also keep a quiet eye on the site in the background, watching uptime, performance, security, and any broken links that may creep in over time. Your website is supposed to be bringing in calls and booking jobs, which means my job does not actually end at launch.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Unlimited content updates included on the monthly plan</li>
          <li>Direct access to me for anything urgent</li>
          <li>Security, uptime, and Lighthouse scores monitored quietly in the background</li>
          <li>Quarterly check-in to talk about what is working and what to add</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

