<section class="section">
  <div class="container text-center" style="max-width:720px">
    <span class="section-label">Process FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-inline:auto">Common process questions.</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I don't have content yet? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I write it for you, and the work flows out of the discovery call rather than out of a blank page. I draft the copy in your voice based on what you told me on the call, send the draft back for review, and we revise it together until each page reads the way you would actually talk to a customer. AI generators tend to produce something generic, which is the opposite of what a service-business site needs. The version we end up with sounds like you, because it came from a real conversation about your work.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I see the site while you are building it? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes, you can, and you genuinely should. I share a live preview link within the first stretch of the build, and you can forward it to anyone whose opinion you want to gather along the way. You stay in the loop for the whole build, not just at the end of it.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How many rounds of revisions do I get? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You get as many revision rounds as you genuinely need, since I do not charge by the change and I do not rush the rounds. I would rather you be happy with the site before it launches than have you discover something to fix the day after it goes live.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I already have a domain? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">That is the most common case, and I handle the DNS switch on launch day so you never have to touch it. The domain stays registered in your name at your registrar throughout, and I simply point it at the new hosting on the day we go live.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What happens to my old website? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I coordinate the cut-over so there is no downtime between the two sites. Once the new one is live, you can take the old one down or keep it archived somewhere private, whichever option you prefer.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

